  "claims": [
    "A supplied contextual higher presentation can realize single separated-exchange generators with checked support. Every existing exchange homotopy then lifts with exactly unchanged support; whole-track exchanges remain derived.",
    "HigherBasis.sum retains both supplied higher presentations on the same first-level rewrite language. Both embeddings preserve all comparison support.",
    "PresentedResidual.Contract permits root-critical comparisons in that supplied presentation, alongside actual target-step embeddings, erased/multiple-step residuals, and separately checked support contracts.",
    "Local root comparisons generate comparisons in all four circuit placements at arbitrary depth and on arbitrary source proof tracks, including formal inverses. The full comparison support equals original path support; residual support is only required to be covered by it.",
    "Rechecking original-path conditions yields a correlated joint-law equality inside the supplied updated checked stateful model, with past, initial shared state and input retained.",
    "The actual MAC instance combines the existing fusion presentation and the unit-critical presentation. MAC contraction, erased unitIdentity and canonical sequential fusion instantiate the same source contract without new arbitrary parallel-path generators.",
    "An actual three-step source path mixes those three root families. Its comparison, including an explicit whole-output sampled-value copy/discard frame, has exactly stage and stage+1 conditions.",
    "The generic joint theorem instantiates from the original checked MAC model through the existing actual structural-rule interpretation.",
    "For the concrete tensor wires identity(finish pair finish) and identity(finish), component normalization followed by the actual canonical tensor normalization has annotation ((4,4),0); direct whole-wire normalization has ((2,2),0). Both values are kernel-proved by reflexivity.",
    "The two concrete tensor normalization paths therefore admit no comparison in the old pure Cartesian.Higher basis. The component path is proved to realize the existing mixed tensorInner obligation after wire-track embedding."
  ],
  "generic_contract": {
    "local_inputs": "A contextual higher presentation, guard-exact realizations of single separated exchange, and for each source root an actual target step, a finite normalized residual path, a higher square and its exact source support.",
    "input_path": "Any source-catalogue rewrite track rho:p->q under arbitrary seq/tensor contexts, with proof composition and formal proof inversion.",
    "output": "A generated PresentedCell iota(rho);nu(q) => nu(p);residual(rho), paired with S(cell)=S(rho).",
    "residual_coverage": "S(residual(rho)) is a subset of S(rho). Erasure does not justify dropping conditions from the comparison.",
    "actual_target": "The old MAC structural/fusion catalogue plus the eighteen-law wire catalogue.",
    "actual_source": "Three schematic root families: MAC contraction, unitIdentity erasure and sequential wire fusion. This is not complete root coverage of the target catalogue."
  },
  "limits": [
    "Canonical tensor-fusion compatibility remains open. Its concrete obstruction concerns only the old pure basis, not the richer mixed or unit-critical presentation. Sufficiency of the single added unit family is not established.",
    "The combined presentation retains the explicit unit comparison, but the displayed mixed normalization proof is not claimed to require or use that unit generator.",
    "The local contracts remain supplied input. The theorem does not construct missing root squares, classify all critical branchings, prove finite complete basis coverage or compare arbitrary parallel source paths.",
    "Guard support is not minimal semantic sensitivity, an encoded certificate bound, a lookup/checking time bound, or an advantage over ordinary proofs with identical sharing/lemmas.",
    "The integer annotation is an algebraic proof-path invariant, not probability, guard count, runtime, security advantage or inequivalence of the underlying wire functions.",
    "Joint equality is inside one updated model, from the original source diagram to the normalized final diagram. It is not arbitrary cross-model equality.",
    "No new code-changing computational reduction, resource/time guarantee, oracle/key-generation execution theorem or MAC advantage bound is derived.",
    "Unregistered NativeConfiguredMAC integration is outside the successful full-library build.",
    "Novelty remains unconfirmed. No new external primary-source reading or independent review occurred in this stage."
  ],
  "next_obligations": [
    "Classify and resolve the actual remaining root-root critical families in the richer basis, rather than assuming pure argument naturality is complete.",
    "Construct the canonical tensor-internal normalization comparison in an adequate explicitly justified presentation, then instantiate its root in PresentedResidual.Contract.",
    "Instantiate association, all pure eighteen-law roots and the remaining fusion/completion roots; establish finite schematic coverage with a precise relation to a genuinely finite basis.",
    "Preserve the original full research scope: computational reductions/losses/resources, continuing execution through oracle internals/keygen, fair total-cost comparison and theorem-level novelty assessment."
  ],
